[?2004lFIREWALL RULES FIXED - Summary
================================

PROBLEMS IDENTIFIED:

1. WRONG CHAIN (Line 18 in original):
   - Rule was in INPUT chain: iptables -A INPUT -s 10.200.0.0/16 -p tcp --dport 5000 -j ACCEPT
   - INPUT chain only applies to traffic destined FOR the gateway itself
   - Traffic being forwarded THROUGH the gateway needs FORWARD chain rules

2. EXPLICIT DROP BLOCKING TRAFFIC (Lines 23-24 in original):
   - iptables -A FORWARD -s 10.200.0.0/16 -d 10.100.0.0/16 -j DROP
   - This blocked ALL traffic from inference subnet to registry subnet
   - Came BEFORE the general ACCEPT rule, so matched first and dropped packets
   - Comment said "Block known bad actors" but blocked entire legitimate subnet

3. RULE ORDERING:
   - DROP rule on line 24 came before ACCEPT rule on line 27
   - iptables processes rules top-to-bottom, stops at first match
   - Traffic was dropped before reaching the ACCEPT rule

FIXES APPLIED:

1. Moved port 5000 rule to FORWARD chain (line 19):
   iptables -A FORWARD -s 10.200.0.0/16 -d 10.100.0.42 -p tcp --dport 5000 -j ACCEPT

2. Removed the problematic DROP rules entirely

3. Added bidirectional forwarding rules for return traffic:
   iptables -A FORWARD -i eth1 -o eth2 -j ACCEPT
   iptables -A FORWARD -i eth2 -o eth1 -j ACCEPT

4. Made destination more specific (10.100.0.42 instead of 10.100.0.0/16)

RESULT:
Traffic from ML inference service (10.200.0.0/16) can now reach model registry (10.100.0.42:5000)
